Ok, so some background here: I've never ascended, but I got a lot (at
least ten) characters to at least the bottom level. Deaths have been
exceedingly stupid these last few runs. I choked on a fortune cookie a
while back -- I think it had something to do with wearing a =oSD... I /
really/ wanted to read that message.

Anyway this time, I start my Chaotic Elven Wizard up. It has a pretty
good starting inventory (Sleep is the best spell to start with) and on
the FIRST level, same room as the upstairs no less, I get an altar,
Magicbane, and holy water. Very soon after that, I find gauntets of
power (I even find a second pair a few levels below that, not that
they were useful for anything...).

Next is a scroll shop which I rob blind in a very exhilirating
manner.

I find a blessed lamp and get a Master Key of Thievery, then ANOTHER
lamp and a silver dragon mail. I'm pretty much set from then on. Down
to Sokoban to get the bag of holding, then to mine's end, getting full
protection on the way.

I get spellbooks of polymorph, identify and finger of death early on,
and once I get the Eye of Aethiopica killing and getting booty become
almost laughably easy. Though I only ever get 1 magic marker in the
game (a polypile) I manage to advance my whole armour to +4 or 5,
including a robe which I got from the priest in the valley of the
dead. My wand of wishes is spent on speed boots, cornuthaum and amulet
of life saving, can't remember what else. I'm set.

About orcus-town is where it gets bad. I'm bored at that time and for
me boredom means stupid mistakes. I accidentally kill a black unicorn
(it looked grey!) then almost immediately afterwards press the wrong
key and pray. Moloch tries to disintegrate me, which I resist (it's
kinda fun surviving an attack by a god, incidentally) and only lose my
robe. No biggie, I put on my old +5 Cloak of MR. Bigger loss is my
protection which I never fully get back.

So I get down to the vibrating square and, knowing I won't have
branchport after the invocation, I go to sokoban to grab the
spellbooks in my stash which I could concievably need on the run.
After that, I decide to maybe run up and fountain-quaff now that I
have skilled spells of remove curse. Next to the Oracle, I my bag of
holding is cursed. I'm stressed from the weight and can't cast remove
curse. I drop the bag. I can't pick it up again. Half numb from shock,
I quit.

Yeah I know I coulda taken stuff out of the bag until I could pick it
up but... the thought of all the stuff vanishing as I did so, and the
thought of how stupid I'd been, I was just so disgusted the quit was
almost reflexive. I recall it was an accidental (subconscious?) button-
mash that brought up the question and a 1-second pause before I go
"yeah, why not? Fuck this!"

Ok, not really a death, but close enough.


